<title>JAPAN: Bank of Japan drains 200 bln yen from market.</title>
<headline>Bank of Japan drains 200 bln yen from market.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Japan (BOJ) drained a net 200 billion yen from the money market on Monday, money traders said.</p>
<p>The drainage left the market with neither a shortfall nor a surplus. It is the first day of the new bank reserve reporting period, they said.</p>
